Z||000005||Fiero_24||09-27-2001||02:45 PM||||I am doing a performance V6 with every mod I can get my hands on.  I am still under the $3000 mark and I have added all new sensors and many more parts.  The only used parts are the block (bored out) heads (performance valve job), injectors (had them tested) and the intake.  The only thing I have to do is put the motor in myself.  I will not be over 200HP, but close.  Yes it is a lot of money to spend on a 2.8, but I like the 2.8 and I think it is worth it.  I will do a V8 eventually, but I want to do one of those right, and for $3000 you cannot I cannot do the really nice V8 I want.  Check out my motor options on my site:  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg">  <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||09-27-2001||02:54 PM||||Formula... you engine is Carbed right?  Not injected. That could be a major difference alone! Mmmm... the power.<P>My 3.1L is running just under (estimated) 200hp, but I'm still getting 16-18mpg around town.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000007||falconhulk||09-27-2001||03:30 PM||||I have a problem in that I have 5 cars and no room to do a conversion.  I was looking for a vendor to do it in my area but aparently no one knows of anyone in Va, PA, MD, or somewhere close.  Not only that the cheapest quote I got from vendors far away was $10,000 for a V8 and $11,000 for 3800!  I sent a response to the 3800 email that i thought it was suppose to be cheaper then the V8 conversion but got no reply.  Dont really have a lot of options at this point.  I was kind of grasping for straws on a 2.8 build up...... as you can see $3000 is a lot better then $10000.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula||09-28-2001||12:24 AM||||yep, I have a carb with a ported and polished intake manifold  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>That does add a lot more enjoyment to the sound at least.  I do think its a lot faster at quarter throttle then the stock 2.8 is floored.<P>falconhulk:  Your probably not more then a hop skip and jump away from me, I hang out in Morgantown WV all the time.  When I bring the fiero out again I'll let you test drive it if you meet me half way.||||reg||1
