Z||000010||Fiero_24||09-28-2001||10:36 AM||||I am taking my 87 GT to WI tonight to start taking the old motor out.  My new motor will be finished in a week or so.  I will let everyone know how well the mods worked out.  I am going to post pics of the motor swap here on the forum once I start it mid October.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||12
Z||000011||Mach10||09-28-2001||11:35 AM||||I'm pretty sure I'm doing a 2.8. I like that motor too. However, if a 3.4tdc drops into my lap for less than my budget ($3000) I'll be doing that. Either way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My 2.8 plans are a complete upper-end, port-polish. The bottom's getting a cross-drilled crank, hi-vol oil pump, a bore-out to 2.9, forged pistons, and a balancing. I'm hoping to kiss 7000rpm. I'm still sourcing the ECM guy in town to make this damn thing work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I'm doing most of the work myself, so I'm 45% sure that this motor will mushroom-cloud on the second run  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
